  "body": "## What happens\n\nA Thread operation on a through hole that `detect_holes` finds does not post. The verification report convicts each helix move with \"move N cuts past the finish surface\".\n\n## How to see it\n\n1. Make a plate 40 x 40 x 10 mm with one through hole, radius 3.3235 mm (96 facets around).\n2. Add the catalog tool `TM-0600-P125`.\n3. Add a Thread operation with the plate as source. Use the hole that `detect_holes` gives (through: true).\n4. Generate and verify.\n\nResult: the verify gate is not empty. Each helix move has the gouge message.\n\n## What we know\n\n- A blind hole of the same radius (`entry_z` at the top, `floor_z` 4.0, `through: false`) verifies and posts without a problem. The test `hole_feed_rating` (PR for #2598) uses that layout for this reason.\n- The cause is not investigated. Possible causes are the helix below the part floor on a through hole, or the finish surface of the faceted hole wall.\n- It is not known if the conviction is correct. If the path really cuts into the wall, the defect is in the generator. If it does not, the defect is in the judgement.\n\n## Expected\n\nA thread mill on a through hole that fits the tool posts, or the refusal names the real cause.\n\nFound during #2598.\n",
